{"name":"Yokohama","slug":"yokohama","region":"East Asia","lat":35.44,"lon":139.64,"seasons":{"DJF":{"season_name":"Dec 2026–Feb 2027","years":[1951,1952,1953,1954,1955,1956,1957,1958,1959,1960,1961,1962,1963,1964,1965,1966,1967,1968,1969,1970,1971,1972,1973,1974,1975,1976,1977,1978,1979,1980,1981,1982,1983,1984,1985,1986,1987,1988,1989,1990,1991,1992,1993,1994,1995,1996,1997,1998,1999,2000,2001,2002,2003,2004,2005,2006,2007,2008,2009,2010,2011,2012,2013,2014,2015,2016,2017,2018,2019,2020,2021,2022,2023,2024,2025],"roni_lead":[-0.38,0.98,0.04,0.84,-0.31,-1.31,-0.14,1.16,0.24,0.04,0.08,-0.16,-0.3,1.06,-0.64,1.86,-0.03,-0.08,0.56,0.67,-0.57,-0.4,1.82,-1.63,-0.45,-0.95,1.04,0.89,-0.08,0.52,-0.06,-0.17,2.03,-0.9,-0.61,-0.18,1.0,1.2,-1.71,-0.23,0.27,1.2,0.1,0.46,0.97,-0.93,-0.25,2.22,-1.33,-1.06,-0.55,-0.18,1.18,0.17,0.7,-0.18,0.73,-1.33,-0.38,0.86,-1.61,-0.91,0.21,-0.22,0.35,2.03,-0.96,-0.82,0.62,0.15,-1.37,-1.08,-1.1,1.3,-0.76],"paragraph":"Dec–Feb in Yokohama has warmed by about 0.2 °C per decade since 1951, roughly 1.4 °C in all, with the coldest days warming fastest, so cold extremes are becoming rarer. There is a clear El Niño signal on temperature: after El Niño conditions in the preceding fall, Dec–Feb tends to run warmer. With this year's strong El Niño, that push is about 50% of a normal year-to-year swing, a noticeable tilt, though ordinary variability can easily outweigh it, roughly as much warmth as 22 years of the long-term trend. Dec–Feb rainfall shows no clear long-term trend, but El Niño may have an effect toward a wetter season with more rainy days, though the evidence is thin, and this year's shift is a noticeable tilt. Relative humidity has fallen by about 0.6 points per decade, roughly 5 points since 1951; because warmer air holds more moisture, this does not necessarily mean the air is drier. El Niño has a strong, well-established effect toward a more humid Dec–Feb, and this year's shift is larger than a normal year-to-year swing. For Dec 2026–Feb 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is likely (about 65% chance), about 0.7 °C above the 1991–2020 average; a more humid season than normal is more likely than not (about 60%). The El Niño expected for Sep–Nov 2026 is stronger than any in the record used here, so the outlook extends the historical relationship beyond what has been observed. This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":7.3676,"trend_per_decade":0.1818,"trend_p":0.0001,"trend_total_since_1951":1.3638,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.239,"enso_p":0.0214,"confidence":"Clear","survives_fdr":false,"fraction_explained":0.0714,"intrinsic_sd":0.8077,"effect_this_season":0.4018,"effect_ratio":0.4974,"size":"Noticeable","size_typical_el_nino":"Noticeable","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":null,"expected_anomaly_2027":0.7232,"forecast_mean":8.0909,"forecast_sd":0.8611,"p_below":0.1111,"p_near":0.2154,"p_above":0.6735,"forecast_words":"Likely (67%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":false,"enso_effect_shrunk_per_degC":0.1588,"shrink_factor":0.6646,"effect_this_season_raw":0.6045,"trend_part_2027":0.3215,"roni_upper_within_record":false,"years_of_warming_equivalent":22.0947,"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.3009,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.2478,"enso_p":0.0689,"confidence":"Suggestive","shift_this_season":0.6269,"lines_cross":false},"p50":{"trend_per_decade":0.1596,"trend_p":0.0002,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.1957,"enso_p":0.0874,"confidence":"Suggestive","shift_this_season":0.4952,"lines_cross":false},"p95":{"trend_per_decade":0.1399,"trend_p":0.0063,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.3965,"enso_p":0.0019,"confidence":"Strong","shift_this_season":1.0032,"lines_cross":false},"tails":{"enso_difference":0.1487,"enso_difference_p":0.3379,"trend_difference":-0.161,"trend_difference_p":0.0089}},"values":[5.337,4.859,5.784,7.318,7.088,6.889,6.367,7.46,7.703,7.498,6.383,7.022,6.